        "fit": "card",
        "label": "Petrus Christus, 1449",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The goldsmith weighs a wedding ring for a richly dressed couple.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "629-the-met-s-goldsmith-got-his-halo-later-1.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "The scales and the ring",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A marriage belt lies across the shop ledge.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "stone",
        "stone": "tanzanite",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "A marriage belt",
        "cut": "oval"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "His shelves hold pearls and coral.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "629-the-met-s-goldsmith-got-his-halo-later-2.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "His shelves",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Among them are fossil shark teeth, believed to protect against poison.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "bracelet",
        "stone": "sapphire",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Shark teeth"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A small round mirror shows two men in the street.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "sapphire",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "label": "A round mirror",
        "cut": "oval"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "For years, he was called Saint Eligius, the goldsmiths' saint.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "629-the-met-s-goldsmith-got-his-halo-later-3.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "With the halo",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A 1990s restoration removed the halo, added by another hand.",
      "say": "A nineteen nineties restoration removed the halo, added by another hand.",
